The dish is a square white plate, roughly 22-24 cm across. On it is a salad of spinach and mixed greens with a few pieces of carrot or orange, some dark beans or olives, and what looks like a light dressing. The greens are piled fairly loosely, so I estimate about 90 g of food in total.

Leafy greens are only about 20-25 kcal per 100 g, so roughly 70 g of greens comes to about 20 kcal. The beans, olives, carrot and other additions add roughly 40 kcal. The dressing and any oil add perhaps 50-60 kcal. That gives a total of about 120 kcal.

